      "source": "stage-intent.ts:33,163; stage-schema.ts:442,678; stage-actions.ts:264,285; stage-panel.tsx:366; collaboration-detail.tsx:70",
      "evidence": "Full and recovery-only records share the existing prefix. Denial removes private body/prose. The strict action union retains exactly the fields needed by the same matcher, and no write body is reconstructed. Reduced objects and stale full handles cannot POST during denial; conflicting stored reduced records also block full-body overwrite. Denied detail exposes original-key GET404/GET200 recovery, with all identity/logout cleanup preserved."
    },
    {
      "id": "C02",
      "status": "resolved",
      "source": "stage-source-cache.ts:15,37; stage-queries.ts:128; stage-code-forms.tsx:35,47",
      "evidence": "R4 source workspace is explicit in keys. A workspace-scoped generation is advanced before cancellation/erasure across same-viewer/session sibling and cross-issue R4 entries. Older success and error are fenced before they can restore evidence or deny issue access. Other workspaces and issue identity survive. Source-dependent forms unmount/remount without their old source snapshots or unsent review text; already-anonymous records preserve their existing read/error state."
    },
    {
      "id": "C03",
      "status": "resolved",
      "source": "stage-code-presentation.ts:28,45; stage-actions.ts:76; stage-code-forms.tsx:40,47",
      "evidence": "Reason-only return derives independently from source-readable approval eligibility. Proper-role/current candidate returns accept null expiry, null evidence and no dependencies; optional hidden references and approval remain blocked. The withheld form exposes no private evidence controls."
    },
    {
      "id": "C04",
      "status": "resolved",
      "source": "stage-code-presentation.ts:29; stage-queries.ts:136; stage-code-forms.tsx:121",
      "evidence": "R1 discovery and R4 must agree on exact candidate identity and current state before authorizing controls. Discovery changes refresh selected R4. Revocation remains separately available for readable superseded, unconsumed decisions."
    },
